*Status update as at 1 August 2024*

{panel:bgColor=#eae6ff}
*Current status*: waiting on new technical implementation details to update Employee Privacy Notice and conduct Privacy Assessments. Discussions are ongoing via Slack with the People Team.
{panel}

* In clause 1.3 of the General Terms and Conditions, the word platform is misspelled and should be corrected.

{color:#36b37e}I do not see any misspellings in English version so please verify is there is any in Azerbaijani one. However, even if it is, there is no need to change it as any misspellings do not have an impact on the meaning of each clause. {color}

* In clause 1.6, the word Buyer should be replaced by the word Customer.

{color:#36b37e}I do not see any misspellings in English version so please verify is there is any in Azerbaijani one. However, even if it is, there is no need to change it as any misspellings do not have an impact on the meaning of each clause. {color}

* There is a conflict between clause 2.3 and clause 2.6.

{color:#36b37e}What kind of conflict? I do not see any. Clause 2.3 refers to limiting the access to the Business Portal, while clause 2.6 refers to suspension of termination of User’s account and its potential consequences.{color}

* It should be clarified what is mentioned in paragraph 2.4.

{color:#36b37e}Basically Bolt allows the Customer to use the Business Portal and Bolt Business within the limits of the Agreement.{color}

-In point 2.3, it is stated that access to the Business Portal will be limited to authorized persons. There is a conflict between the current clause and clause 2.3, which should be clarified.

{color:#36b37e}As above, I do not understand this comment and I do not see any conflict (and with what?).{color}

-Clause 3.1. The service fee will be made based on the relevant payment documents that will be presented to the Customer. According to the current situation, Bolt has no such right in relation to a customer who is a legal entity.

{color:#36b37e}I cannot see anything like this in clause 3.1. Has client reviewed the appropriate T&Cs? Nevertheless, the Customer is defined in point 1.5 as a company or other person, so there is relation to a legal entity (company).{color}

* A comment has been added regarding the "provider of transport, sale, delivery or rental services" mentioned in clause 3.5. Is the provider of the mentioned services another person?

{color:#36b37e}Again, I cannot see anything like this in clause 3.5. Nevertheless, yes. Bolt is only a platform provider, we do not provide any other services, e.g. transportation.{color}

* In paragraph 3.6, the word "fees" is written incorrectly and should be corrected.

{color:#36b37e}I do not see any misspellings in English version so please verify is there is any in Azerbaijani one. However, even if it is, there is no need to change it as any misspellings do not have an impact on the meaning of each clause. {color}

* In subsection 4.1.1, the word "by" should be added after the word "Bolt", and the letter "i" should be deleted in the word "data".

{color:#36b37e}I do not see any misspellings in English version so please verify is there is any in Azerbaijani one. However, even if it is, there is no need to change it as any misspellings do not have an impact on the meaning of each clause. {color}

* In clause 6.3, the second word "damages" shall be deleted.

{color:#36b37e}I do not see any misspellings in English version so please verify is there is any in Azerbaijani one. However, even if it is, there is no need to change it as any misspellings do not have an impact on the meaning of each clause. {color}

* In clause 7.1, it is appropriate to state that "the Agreement shall enter into force from the moment it is signed and sealed by both parties".

{color:#36b37e}Not in this case. The Customer has to sing up at Business Portal.{color}

* In paragraph 7.4, the wording of the Agreement is written incorrectly and should be corrected.

{color:#36b37e}I do not see any misspellings in English version so please verify is there is any in Azerbaijani one. However, even if it is, there is no need to change it as any misspellings do not have an impact on the meaning of each clause.{color}

* Clause 7.5. What constitutes a significant breach?

{color:#36b37e}This is determined case by case. e.g. granting an access to the Business Portal to non-authorized party.{color}

* In clause 8.2, after the word "data", the word "through" should be added.

{color:#36b37e}I do not see any misspellings in English version so please verify is there is any in Azerbaijani one. However, even if it is, there is no need to change it as any misspellings do not have an impact on the meaning of each clause. {color}
It should be clarified what is mentioned in clause 8.7.

-Clause 1.1 of the Special Terms should state that "These Special Terms shall come into force upon both signature and seal." marking it as is appropriate for the purpose.

{color:#36b37e}Not in this case. The Customer has to sing up at Business Portal.{color}

* In paragraph 2.5, the following statement should be added "The customer must check the submitted payment documents within 15 working days after receiving the statement, e-receipt and invoice, and if there are no discrepancies, make the payment. If the customer discovers a discrepancy after checking the account statement, e-receipt and invoice, he must inform Bolt within 10 working days, and the investigation and elimination of those discrepancies must be completed within 5 working days."

{color:#36b37e}We cannot agree on such clause. The Customer has to make the payment but we can investigate discrepancies after so we can add the following sentence “If the customer discovers a discrepancy after checking the account statement, e-receipt and invoice, he must inform Bolt within 10 working days, and the investigation and elimination of those discrepancies must be completed within 10 working days”{color}

* Clause 2.6 should be deleted.

{color:#36b37e}We cannot remove clause 2.6. This will only apply in case of late payments so it will not apply as long as the Customer pays its liabilities on time.{color}

