* only a few clauses (Part A clause 11, Part B clause 16 of the T&C) seem to generally only cover confidentiality & personal data transfer of employees/representatives for the purpose of preparing and concluding the contract. The clauses are very vague and restrictive in some parts for Bolt.
* additionally, clause 16(5) of the Exhibit B of the T&C requires the parties to conclude a separate contract to process personal data, but its not included.

The light touch clauses for data controllers added [*this agreement*|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Qi7nz4yOrDAYW8NaQSB-DLZ7rHBmhx4l/edit] by [~accountid:712020:8c797c70-7a57-496e-aa3f-5d91df806eb2] would formally suffice, if the transfer is only limited to employees/representatives data. Additionally, we would ideally have to request to remove some restricting provisions in the T&Cs.

Examples form Part B clause 16 of the T&C: 

{panel:bgColor=#deebff}
_The Supplier (Bolt) shall comply with the Corporate Information Security and Data Protection Policy, ST shall have the right to inspect/audit independently or through a third party the compliance with the specified security measures._
{panel}

We do no want to be subject to their policies🔼 

{panel:bgColor=#deebff}
In the event that the Subcontractor should have access to … [personal data]… the Supplier (Bolt) is obliged to inform ST of this fact in advance.
{panel}

Not sure if this will apply, but we will not specifically inform ST that subcontractors received access to their personal data🔼

