Following a 1:1 comparison between {{provider index}} and {{provider alternative index}}, there are a couple of fields that are only stored in documents from {{provider alternative index}} : 

{noformat}coverage: {
    coordinates: {
        lat: number;
        lon: number;
    };
    range: number;
}{noformat}

While the {{coordintes}} filed is present in both indexes, the {{range}} field is present only in {{provider-alt}} index. However, it seems that the {{range}} value is always set to 0 (see all conversion methods from src/delivery/eater/delivery_eater_data_store/main/elastic_index/provider/ProviderAlternativeIndex.ts), so I would argue it is safe not to include it in {{provider index}}



→ Another difference is the fact that {{provider alternative index}} stores all tag related data, while {{provider index}} stores only {{tag ids}}. However:

* Our non tag specific endpoints return only tag ids
* We have an ES index for provider tags which is currently in used and all searches used with {{provider alternative index}} make use of ids only

  As a result, there is no need to change the {{provider index}} to store anything other than tag ids.



→ The alternative index also contains an ancient field called {{blanket_menu_discount}} which is only stored, but a quick search in ES shows that there are currently no documents with this field. It shouldn’t be used anymore so I deem it safe to not have it on {{provider-index}} 

→ {{price_level}} ([https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/ST/pages/1220446939/Restaurant+price+level+...+-+Idea+Phase|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/ST/pages/1220446939/Restaurant+price+level+...+-+Idea+Phase|smart-link] )

{noformat}    export enum PriceLevel {
        ONE = "one",
        TWO = "two",
        THREE = "three"
    }{noformat}

This field is returned as part of the {{Provider}} and {{ProviderSummary}} interfaces ({{"/internal/findProviderSummaries"}}). It does not exist on {{provider index}} but it should be added as it is just an enum with 3 values (for the moment)



→ {{hide_out_of_serving_interval}} & {{hide_out_of_serving_interval_dishes_in_eater_app}} 

On {{provider}} index we have {{hide_oot_dishes: provider.hide_out_of_serving_interval_dishes_in_eater_app}}

{{ProviderDetails}} from {{DeliveryProviderInternalAsyncApi}} has 2 values:

{noformat}{
  hide_out_of_serving_interval: boolean;
  hide_out_of_serving_interval_dishes_in_eater_app: boolean;
}{noformat}

The interesting bit is that while for {{provider_index}} the {{hide_out_of_serving_interval_dishes_in_eater_app}} is used as expected, for {{provider-alternative}} both values use the {{hide_out_of_interval}} and it seems that only the {{hide_out_of_serving_interval_dishes_in_eater_app}} is used in the logic. This seems to be a bug.

As a fix, we could store the {{hide_out_of_serving_interval}} value on {{provider index}}, but it might not be necessary. I’ve asked the provider team what is the meaning of each of the two values, and I am waiting for a reply.

→ {{order_type: DeliveryOrderType;}} The only order type we currently support is {{DeliveryOrderType.Parallel}} and I think it is safe to not store this anymore

→ There is also a small discrepancy in the way we store the traits related data on each of the index. For {{provider-alt}} index we also store the name of the trait, while for {{provider}} index we don’t as all searches / filters happen either by {{trait_slug}} or {{trait_id}}. I think we can continue to do it this way and no updates would be required.

→ Last field of interest is the {{images}} field, which does not exist on the {{provider index}}. There is an {{image}} field that stores only one image path (see below). But the entire structure is a bit more complex with some metadata etc and it is also returned as part of the {{"/internal/findProviderSummaries"}} response. A bit more investigation is required, but I would store this in the {{provider index}} just to be on the safe side.

